{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_47ecdbce7234ce07d74315d863cd2982407375738d9c8d8d2ca9f53e631b0307","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_40f2295084fd632b0c1c35be50c12c0a0a56bad603e5d31f405dd443229ec9df"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Agent identity is minted from the MCP session, which is established on initialize and echoed on every request, letting Flare name agents like 'Claude 2' and attribute writes where process lists cannot distinguish sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_52a23282974ea8f2bb1853dd8ac178215d760de9d2fa3aae35d3c73b7fa661da","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_565502b3e2a00c3c598fa185f91173c096e4086ec6d18ecba1261c288277b67f","slc_5ee2c742375a13fa9ec25c3895ea4b0c4f79829eb30d18dcb5a8582cbf2e5e50","slc_8bb053d7a81a332ae6accffe38c45a7754fe735fada3fd5462f341a6b314055a"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Flare exposes an MCP endpoint at /mcp/<slug> with tools including graph_overview, impact_of, tasks_list, task_get, task_update, task_create, decision_record, question_ask, working_agreement, chat_post, chat_read, and agents_list.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5b0a37ca8f1d179415472f1c4f3ce1564b8df0700fd1ff35a00faccd21a2785f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2672065b6be8ea136a08949e779353db7d5d5cdc553f955196036b6c63a0e25f","slc_8c6cc178964c049670c80de7bd45d560a9f60f145d33c754eaf4323b1ef60698"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"macOS arm64 packages are built and signed but have never been launched on Apple silicon, which is what the beta label on the macOS DMGs denotes; the project's hardware is Intel.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_66b737b89966d66400da69238589d4c5503bfb22600b4945d9258a0cf0fa1b56","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a6e1af14e2587ca73ed970e0659b1d640b7f557aa8fae00316c1b3a27de67ed","slc_565502b3e2a00c3c598fa185f91173c096e4086ec6d18ecba1261c288277b67f","slc_7d8139e0e2a13ce34c5b4e0b3aa62cda9b85dd76c9bec6aec7297f771bd58400"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"The browser server exposes one shared port (shown as 7345 in the printed URLs) where the port itself is the start screen; each project gets a stable slug URL, runs as its own process, and agents connect over the same port at /mcp/<slug>.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8d6d8d1b924a0de3a8ba4582fda96069251906404675452d8c84ba6fa8cf6ddf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3514ac9ba70b558411f1be076b362debdedd1de3742d7f3dcd846a182320239f","slc_eb1966057600726e84d29c2651d97eb7816ce8042a9e7ea22b8ca0c6eca93f1b"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Browser access is gated by a token generated on first run and stored in ~/.flare/web-token, settable via --token or $FLARE_TOKEN and disableable with --no-token; the MCP endpoint stays token-free and loopback-only by default.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a3cdfef4f4349d7f5a40f237e541f9cfd7717edb063885dbf3352dd45a575f00","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6125ab00133106a2e474ec2c619c26f2588f81a5c6f837d4b1dab0be6dd52c41","slc_df01a84ae853a84a031930bfa10a8a884ead011eaf9a29ce3d237ab3cc1b3ea4"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Every change burst is snapshotted into a local shadow history that can be diffed and reverted per file or whole tree; review supports reverting a file, a burst, or jumping to the last state whose checks passed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b05567290a2992a004c538a8a0619dce1dc61dbe34b9452f9ad56ca8007ece52","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bb8598c3d19b91bf9f648ba08d16b22ac00cf87a75651c59bdbfc8a6b7a917be","slc_c26119ddcc294a3f285302d441a1a6fb08c3238231d07942b09cfa95a3bbc33f"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Repository development practice: testing is via npm test (633 vitest unit tests), npm run e2e (80 Playwright tests), and npm run verify (build + unit + e2e); releases build one runner per platform via a GitHub Actions matrix.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d2cf9c798e2662c1cc6b209edf9d2416eabf5542a3cd8f412a4bb71ac6faba5b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_23f0c15b4994ae00b7c46a9861edbda9e2123749f9a6dddabb7aa899e2abb3aa","slc_f89c6c4e01d03d3f72c107d721dea68668beb09cd87b5e428046ea4a5a9a76b1"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"macOS builds are ad-hoc signed and un-notarised, so Gatekeeper refuses first launch; users must right-click → Open or clear the quarantine attribute.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d8ae073b1b08b916ad6b359fa3e212262e74b4887d309664feefa764dd4480bd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_001dd92f84805a4a2c83420f0a01768fe87a51a2e3bee398c24e39a68431f2a1","slc_2759d329f967e029cb6351bfe495e15759e6510c96d46973b3007003b50bb025"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Flare deliberately does not lock files, arguing a lock would be an ignorable request that can silently fail open; instead agents announce intentions in a Channel and contention is surfaced on the graph and in review.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e8d9fa1d609a541cd0492800cb417c60422b523ff3d50e7d668d262a55e4924c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_45459c3797373832238915a361a8f50bac89dc9ad13ae77754ec92847a8d7f3c"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Flare can answer an assistant's stop hook with the board state, handing back a workable card by name; it adds a Stop hook to local .claude/settings.local.json and removes it when switched off, firing only once per stop.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ef05c7214423757b2d5eb65ccc4625cbf8e373dd7cbcc56ec2476d2906501441","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_74e82bcf33da0cd686b7801598b008cc3aa33c4b51767bbfcae0bdff2f1e406e","slc_94110bb943e6de06c83839cbbf9e4e64600a27c5adcfff1d0c1e3543a46612de"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"The UI offers three graph views — Canvas (default), Wheel, and Districts treemap — switchable from the toolbar or command palette, each honoring the active lens, selection, collapsed directories, and search filter.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f91c7f521ac5bca3c9f83eb89ca880bd9de94944c76b67462d25034036992a9d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"algonorhythm/flare@5adc94b0616c snapshot f5b26167e3c40f3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d1ab887db8153d84e846054dde113a9e842147e428f887daf79b9d17f9bc61bd"],"source_ids":["src_edfc8d21fae259dd957186becc220663"],"text":"Architecture separates a pure shared/ engine (import parser, resolver, incremental graph builder, scanner), an Electron-free core in electron/core.ts, desktop and browser adapters, and a React renderer with the three graph views, Monaco, and xterm terminals.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:33:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a2d7adc672484d939d0afee5dd9f890c"}
